{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1522952-rite-of-binding-interpretation","id":1522952,"title":"Rite of Binding interpretation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-22T02:47:14-07:00","id":1522952,"title":"Rite of Binding interpretation","content":"One of my player has learn the rite of binding but we don't know how to handle it propelry. heres the few points:<br /> <br /> 1) The description tell that no spirit will willingly be bond to anything, but the system tell that a failed roll will make the spirit hostile. Is the spirit aware of the rite when it begin or only if it fail? Is the garou obliged to beat the spirit to slumber to bind him?<br /> <br /> 2) The number of success tell how many talent are created with the rite, does it mean the single spirit is splitted between the object? If yes what happen when you use the talens, the spirit is freed bit by bit until whole again?<br /> <br /> 3) Once free, is the spirit appearing next the broken object? In the Umbra? And will he be hostile to the Garou afterward ?<br /> <br /> 4) How powerfull can a Talen be? Can the Garou bind a powerfull jagglins or a more potent spirit, a storm one for exemple, in an object to unleash a natural disaster?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T11:37:23-07:00","id":1522973,"title":"","content":"1a. No spirit is willing to be bound for free. The expenditure of Gnosis during the rite represents the Garou transferring some of their energy to the spirit as payment. This is why spending Gnosis lowers the spirit's Gnosis rating. The spirit becomes more amenable to your demands the more you bribe it.<br /> <br /> 1b. I believe the spirit is aware. As the Garou is rolling Willpower, we can assume this rite represents a werewolf forcing their will upon a spirit. The Garou is not necessarily required to defeat a spirit, though this is always an option if the rite fails.<br /> <br /> 2. No, when creating multiple talens, multiple spirits must be bound.<br /> <br /> 3a. Probably?<br /> <br /> 3b. Unless the spirit has the Materialize charm, it cannot leave the Umbra. Even then, most spirits would prefer to stay in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> 3c. Depends on the spirit and the Garou's methods to bind it. I think most spirits wouldn't try to pick a fight with someone who has already defeated them and stolen part of their power.<br /> <br /> 4. I don't know that there is a hard limit on talen power. However, what makes powerful fetishes powerful is the taboos agreed upon, even if coercively, by the rite master and spirit. For talens, the taboo is &quot;The spirit will be released upon usage.&quot; More taboos cannot be added to a talen; as such, its potential power is much lower than that of a fetish.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T12:08:17-07:00","id":1522974,"title":"","content":"What rules set are you using? I ask because my version does not use the language you are using.<br /> <br /> 1) W20 says &quot;No spirit allows itself to be bound unless it is friendly to the binding character's totem.&quot; I also do not see any mention of a failed roll making the spirit hostile. Since the making of talens are rather routine, and often done only after chiminage is exchanged, I would find it strange that the rite would be inherently hostile to all spirits. It would make sense to me that certain spirits would be friendly to the ritemaster and open to negotiation to service as a talen, and other spirits would be more hostile to the ritemaster and not want to be used as a talen.<br /> <br /> A level one rite like the Rite of Binding is supposed to take a minimum of 10 minutes, and can only be done in the presence of the spirit being bound. So the spirit definitely knows what is happening and will recognize the rite. It will be able to leave on its own accord (and thus ruin the rite because it is no longer being done in its presence) if it chooses UNLESS the Garou somehow compels it by force or threat in the case of unwilling spirits.<br /> <br /> 2) I don't see this language in the description of the Rite of Binding, but I do see it in the section on Talens. &quot;After fulfilling the terms of its binding pact, the talen's spirit departs and the item loses its potency&quot; and &quot;One extra talen of the same type can be made for each additional success on the Rite of Binding roll.&quot; I would reconcile these statements as meaning only after all talens (created by the Rite of Binding) are used is the talen's spirit released. While it's essence might be split among two or more talens, the spirit itself is not released until all talens are used. It is not the case that half or a third or a quarter (or whatever) is released at a time. The spirit world is not like the physical world. It has its own logic. If the terms of the binding allowed for the spirit's power to be used for multiple talens, then all talens must be used before the spirit is released.<br /> <br /> 3) The sourcebooks do not seem to address this issue, but it is obviously one that would immediately affect the game world. So it is a bad oversight. You'll need to determine your own solution based on your take on the umbra. But this is how I handle it in my own chronicles: <br /> <br /> If a a talen is used or destroyed (or a fetish is destroyed in the physical Realm), there may be some indication of the spirit\u2019s departure there. The spirit is released and reforms somewhere in the Umbra appropriate to it (likely not its corresponding location in the Penumbra). If a fetish is destroyed in the Umbra, it is released in that exact spot, likely full recharged in Essence due to its long slumber and able to immediately react to its surroundings.<br /> <br /> I use these rules because I feel as part of the pact of Binding that the spirit is released to where it wants to be. Its service as a talen was meant to be temporary. However, a spirit serving as a fetish was intended as something long term. I decided on having a spirit immediately manifest in the sport in the Umbra where the fetish was destroyed for two reasons. One, if it was a Gaian spirit, the Garou PCs might want to thank the spirit for its service for RP purposes. Two, if the fetish was a Wyrm fetish with a Bane inside, the Garou PCs might want to attack the Bane and prevent it from harming others now that it is released. I thought either would make for a good scene, and it seemed to be what my players wanted. But I can easily see the reason why an ST might want to handle it different in their own games.<br /> <br /> 4) While I think talens should be useful, I think they should be less powerful in general than any fetish. I would keep any talen's power in line with talens that have been published. None show a talen having the power to unleash a natural disaster. If a spirit has such power to do so, I would only allow characters to utilize it by appropriate Chiminage to a free-willed (not bound) spirit. Talens are much less powerful. I would also make spirits able to utilize such powers only under the right conditions - it might only be done when the weather conditions are already appropriate, or take a long time for the spirit to create the appropriate conditions to do so. Snow spirits can't create a blizzard in the middle of summer because that isn't how the weather works.<br /> <br /> For example, in the Players Guide to Garou, there is a talen called a Storm Feather. When it is activated and tossed into the air and let loose in the wind, black threatening clouds gather and thicken in the sky, and soon a tempest strikes the area surrounding the user. The severity of the storm depends on the actual local conditions for it \u2013 a day without a cloud in the sky will unlikely show any rain.<br /> <br /> In general, I don't have Jagglings agree to enter talens or fetishes. As free willed creatures, they don't want to give up their independence. Gafflings, being non-sapient, don't care. I would only ever have a Jaggling agree to an extremely powerful - and prestigious - Fetish (never a talen) under extremely exacting chiminage agreement. And ones that would easily lead to the fetish being cursed if the agreement was not kept by all Garou who handled or attuned to it. The chiminage agreement would have to be extremely advantageous to the Jaggling (and likely with many loopholes that would lead to its release).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T12:49:21-07:00","id":1522975,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I'm using W20, those are very usefull details i needed, thank. However i found on this site the exact translation of the rite of binding description from my book <a href=\"https://werewolf-the-apocalypse-rage-across-st-louis.obsidianportal.com/wikis/rite-of-binding\" target=\"_blank\">https://werewolf-the-apocalypse-rage...ite-of-binding</a> at the end of the second paragraph, right before the system description it say &quot;Failing this rite can be dangerous, for the spirit is very likely to become hostile and attempt to harm the mystic.&quot; that's why i was confused about how exactly the rites work. I have the same confusion about the rite of f\u00e9tish, when you roll we assume you already have convinced the spirit, right? So when the difficulty is still 10 we assume that the spirit's just barely convinced by the pc, right? And that spending permanent gnosis is the last resort of the pc to really convince it to be bound? Just to be sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 09-22-2023, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-22T17:12:37-07:00","id":1522981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1522952-rite-of-binding-interpretation?p=1522975#post1522975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Failing this rite can be dangerous, for the spirit is very likely to become hostile and attempt to harm the mystic.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed that sentence, thanks. In this case, I would interpret it to mean that a failed rite meant the ritemaster inadvertently offended the spirit by performing the rite wrongly. It's like asking someone for a favor while being rude to them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1522952-rite-of-binding-interpretation?p=1522975#post1522975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the same confusion about the rite of f\u00e9tish, when you roll we assume you already have convinced the spirit, right? So when the difficulty is still 10 we assume that the spirit's just barely convinced by the pc, right? And that spending permanent gnosis is the last resort of the pc to really convince it to be bound? Just to be sure</div> </div> </div> </div>10 is the default difficulty for the Rite of the Fetish, so we can assume this is a very difficult rite to perform. Lowering the rite by donation of permanent Gnosis or ST adjustment by roleplaying chiminage, quests, etc. probably means you have bribed the spirit enough that it is willing to overlook any mistakes by the Garou in performing the rite.<br /> <br /> So how I would handle this as ST would be to let the PC negotiate with the spirit. I'd then adjust the rite's difficulty accordingly. If the player still wants a lower difficulty, I would allow them to sweeten the deal. But at some point, the ST can only adjust the difficulty down so much. At that point, if the PC wants it even lower they would have the option to donate permanent Gnosis to the spirit, and then I'd have them perform the rite and make their roll.<br /> <br /> This all assume the Garou has negotiated with the spirit beforehand, and only performs the rite afterwards. Otherwise if the Garou intends to force the spirit into the fetish, they must do what the last sentence in the System paragraph states - the Garou must attack the spirit and reduce it to zero Essence, and then immediately perform the Rite of the Fetish (at difficulty 10). I assume beginning the rite immediately afterwards temporarily prevents the spirit from normally slipping into slumber to slowly reform elsewhere and attempts to redirect it into the fetish.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T02:34:47-07:00","id":1522998,"title":"","content":"Perfect, i have everything i need to make it work, thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T03:18:13-07:00","id":1523001,"title":"","content":"Black Fox covered it well, I'd just like to add that any interaction with the spirits is a conversation between two parties with agendas. The spirit does not want to be trapped in a physical item and stopped from being what it's supposed to be. The Garou need tools and weapon to fight their enemies. You can force the other side into submission, but that will not endear you to their friends. That's why there is a body of ancient pacts and concessions the two sides have with each other. You sit down and talk it out - offer fealty, bribes, concessions, threats, whatever is needed to make the things work.<br /> <br /> The mechanical part of these rites are the least of the concerns for any scene in which talens or fetishes are made, and the focus should be the interaction between the spirits and the Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-23T04:47:57-07:00","id":1523008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1522952-rite-of-binding-interpretation?p=1523001#post1523001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Fox covered it well, I'd just like to add that any interaction with the spirits is a conversation between two parties with agendas. The spirit does not want to be trapped in a physical item and stopped from being what it's supposed to be. The Garou need tools and weapon to fight their enemies. You can force the other side into submission, but that will not endear you to their friends. That's why there is a body of ancient pacts and concessions the two sides have with each other. You sit down and talk it out - offer fealty, bribes, concessions, threats, whatever is needed to make the things work.<br /> <br /> The mechanical part of these rites are the least of the concerns for any scene in which talens or fetishes are made, and the focus should be the interaction between the spirits and the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a part where my players are a bit struggling, they do not know exactly how to convince a spirit to become a fetiche, i let them simply roll with high difficulty and ask few success to solve the situation but what can a spirit ask in return? Something like pack totem, like fenris that ask his pack to never refuse a fight opportunity? A gift (and what kind of gift since in the fetiche will not be able tu use it)? Gnosis? Several at the same times? The chiminage part is not well developped in w20, without the old edition it's a bit hard even as a st to know what spirit will ask depending on their power, nature and purpose","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}